{
  "name": "m4-split-panes",
  "description": "M4 gate (m4-split-panes sub-spec 7): two fixture sites side by side, keyboard only. prefix+v and prefix+- give an L shape; h/j/k/l move focus by geometry with MRU, and each pane keeps its own mode (b has a focused input: insert); z zooms and unzooms; shift+h swaps; resize mode l l gives 60/40; a screenshot of the result; Enter in b's input goes DOM fullscreen (b fills the 1280x800 window) and back to the same layout; x closes a pane and keeps its tab; a second workspace keeps its own split across ctrl+b ( and ctrl+b ); and the zoomed layout survives ctrl+q and a start on the same profile. Each page titles itself with its width, so state's titles check the geometry. Prefs: Vimma's own browser.startup.page (resume the session); full-screen-api.ignore-widgets, since Xvfb has no window manager to make the window fullscreen (the window already fills the screen). The status bar shows the fixture server's fixed port (28471).",
  "timeoutSeconds": 120,
  "prefs": {
    "browser.startup.page": null,
    "full-screen-api.ignore-widgets": true
  },
